# `data/` and `models/` are build outputs and stay out of the build context
# entirely. The image does not copy them from the host -- it builds them, in the
# `databuild` stage, from `meridian-account-health.zip`.
#
# That is not a stylistic preference. `.gitignore` excludes these paths, so they
# do not exist in a clone, and a hosting platform builds from a clone. Copying
# them from the host would produce an image that builds on the machine that
# happens to have run `make bootstrap` and fails everywhere else -- which is
# precisely the shape of bug that only shows up on the deployment.
data
models

# `artifacts` is NOT excluded: it is committed, it is under a megabyte, and
# `GET /api/evaluations/{name}` reads it. Without it a deployment reports every
# evaluation as never run while the repository publishes their numbers.

logs
*.docx
# Every zip except the source archive, which the `databuild` stage extracts.
*.zip
!meridian-account-health.zip
.env
